+# Runbook: MCP + A2A + n8n integration (overview)
+
+1) Deploy n8n:
+   - helm upgrade --install n8n helm/n8n -f helm/n8n/values.yaml --namespace aegis-ops --create-namespace
+   - Apply external secret to provide basic auth: kubectl apply -f k8s/n8n/external-secret-n8n.yaml
+
+2) Deploy MCP service:
+   - kubectl apply -f mcp/server/main.py (containerize in production)
+   - Set MCP_API secret in GitHub to http(s) endpoint of MCP service
+
+3) Wire CI to publish MCP:
+   - Use .github/workflows/publish_mcp.yml to create+sign MCP record during promotion
+   - Ensure COSIGN_KEY and MCP_API are set as repository secrets
+
+4) Deploy A2A topics and consumer:
+   - kubectl apply -f a2a/strimzi/topics.yaml (requires Strimzi)
+   - Deploy approver consumer as a k8s Deployment (containerize a2a/consumer/approver_consumer.py)
+
+5) Example flows:
+   - TRT bake: n8n workflow trt_bake_trigger.json triggers bake and posts approval request to approver (via API) or publishes to a2a topic using the agent SDK.
+   - Approval: approver consumes messages, writes approvals to DB; once approvals reach multisig threshold, MCP record is updated with approval sigs.
+
+6) Evidence:
+   - Run ops/compliance/evidence_mcp_a2a.py to collect MCP and A2A artifacts for auditors.
+
